<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Satrae</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Satrae were a Thracian people of the mountains of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> hinterland, described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> in the 5th century BCE as the only <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thracians">Thracians</a> never to have been subjected. They held an oracle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dionysus">Dionysus</a> on a high mountain, where members of the Bessi served as prophets. They are not clearly attested in later sources.</p></div>
